# Case mapping covers all of Unicode, and comes in two flavours.
#
# A Char maps 1:1 — `Char -> Char` cannot expand — so it takes the SIMPLE
# mapping and `'ß'.upperCase` is `'ß'`. A String takes the FULL mapping and may
# grow, so `"ß".upperCase` is `"SS"`. Both are per codepoint and
# locale-independent, so the Greek final sigma does NOT become a medial one.
#
# The tables are generated by tools/unicode_case_gen.py and were diffed against
# OTP's `string:uppercase/1` over all 1.1M codepoints. BEAM's Char path used to
# be `string:to_upper/1`, which is the pre-Unicode function and mapped only
# ISO-8859-1 — everything below outside Latin-1 was a silent no-op there.

main do
  # Beyond Latin-1: Greek and Cyrillic, as Char and as String
  IO.printLine("${'α'.upperCase} ${'Ω'.lowerCase} ${'д'.upperCase} ${'Я'.lowerCase}")
  IO.printLine("${"αβγ".upperCase} ${"ΑΒΓ".lowerCase}")
  IO.printLine("${"привет".upperCase} ${"ПРИВЕТ".lowerCase}")

  # Latin Extended-A pairs, and a stroke letter whose pair is not adjacent
  IO.printLine("${"ā ł ż".upperCase} ${"Ā Ł Ż".lowerCase}")

  # A String may grow; the same character as a Char may not.
  IO.printLine("${"straße".upperCase} / ${'ß'.upperCase}")
  IO.printLine("${"ﬁn".upperCase} / ${'ﬁ'.upperCase}")

  # Per codepoint, so a trailing sigma lower-cases to the medial form —
  # matching string:lowercase/1 rather than a context-sensitive mapping.
  IO.printLine("${"ΟΔΟΣ".lowerCase}")

  # Caseless scripts pass through untouched
  IO.printLine("${"日本語 עברית".upperCase}")

  # Round trip through chars/map keeps a String a String
  IO.printLine("${"éclair".chars.map(&.upperCase).join("")}")
end
